{"abstract":"WNTs are lipid-modified proteins that control multiple functions in development and disease via short- and long-range signaling. However, it is unclear how these hydrophobic molecules spread over long distances in the mammalian brain. Here we show that WNT5A is produced by the choroid plexus (ChP) of the developing hindbrain, but not the telencephalon, in both mouse and human. Since the ChP produces and secretes the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF), we examine the presence of WNT5A in the CSF and find that it is associated with lipoprotein particles rather than exosomes. Moreover, since the CSF flows along the apical surface of hindbrain progenitors not expressing Wnt5a, we examined whether deletion of Wnt5a in the ChP controls their function and find that cerebellar morphogenesis is impaired. Our study thus identifies the CSF as a route and lipoprotein particles as a vehicle for long-range transport of biologically active WNT in the central nervous system.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Kaiser, Karol","Gyllborg, Daniel","Procházka, Jan","Salasova, Alena","Kompaníková, Petra","Molina, Francisco Lamus","Laguna-Goya, Rocio","Radaszkiewicz, Tomasz","Harnoš, Jakub","Procházková, Michaela","Potěšil, David","Barker, Roger A.","Casado, Ángel Gato","Zdráhal, Zbyněk","Sedláček, Radislav","Arenas, Ernest","Villaescusa, J. Carlos","Bryja, Vítězslav"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-167236"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Villaescusa, J. Carlos"],"country":["Czechia","Spain","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Central European Institute of Technology","Karolinska Institutet","Masaryk University","University of Valladolid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"wnt000000000005a is transported via lipoprotein particles in the cerebrospinal fluid to regulate hindbrain morphogenesis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-019-09298-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-167236","identifier":[{"id":"30940800","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6445127","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85063737300","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4292282c-83b8-4cbe-b27b-bd55f39556b9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-556593A2327E3B135AA663543797805C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-019-09298-4","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Skou-bygningen","Aarhus University, Interfaculty Centre, DANDRITE, DANDRITE - Nykjær Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cz","key":"masaryk university","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Masaryk University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"university of valladolid","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OE